      "text": "Since the binomials have integer coefficients, their sum and product must be integers. Therefore, the product $(-1)(2008)$ must equal the product of two binomials having integer coefficients.\nIt is easy to see that the factorization of the given polynomial is $(x+p)(x+q)$ where $p-q=b$. Substituting for $p$ and $q$ you get $pq=-2008$, so $p+q=-63$. $(p−q)^2=p^2−2pq+q^2=2008+2(p^2+q^2)$.\nNote that $p+q=−63$ and $pq=−2008$ implies $p^2+q^2=(p+q)^2−2pq=3509$. Plugging into the previous equation gives $(−64)^2=2008$, which gives $−64^2=2008$. We get that $8^2$ must be less.\n9$,$ the smallest possible positive integer, is $\\boxed{8}$. The answer is 8",
