      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve for the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) such that \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) can be expressed as a product of two binomials with integer coefficients, we need to determine the possible integer pairs \\((p, q)\\) such that:\n\n\\[ x^2 + bx + 2008 \\]\n\ncan be factored as:\n\n\\[ (x + p)(x + q) \\]\n\nwhere:\n\n\\[ p \\cdot q = 2008 \\]\n \nand\n\n\\[ b = p + q \\]\n\nWe must find the pair of integers \\((p, q)\\) whose product is 2008, and then find their sum, which will give us the value of \\( b \\). Let's start by factoring 2008 into its factors.\n\n### Step-by-Step Solution:\n\n1. **Find the factors of 2008**: \n   \\[\n   2008 = 2^3 \\times 251\n   \\]\n\n2. **List all possible pairs \\((p, q)\\) such that \\( p \\times q = 2008 \\)**:\n   These pairs are all combinations of the factors of 2008.\n\n3. **Calculate \\( b = p + q \\) for these pairs**:\n   We need to identify the smallest positive value of \\( b \\) from these sums.\n\nLet's use Python to accurately identify these pairs and compute the sums.\n```python\nimport itertools\nimport math\n\n# Function to list all pairs of factors of 2008\ndef factor_pairs(n):\n    factors = []\n    for i in range(1, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            j = n // i\n            factors.append((i, j))\n    return factors\n\n# Function to find the sum of pairs\ndef sum_of_pairs(pairs):\n    return [sum(pair) for pair in pairs]\n\n# List all factor pairs\npairs = factor_pairs(2008)\n\n# Find the largest sums\ns = sum_of_pairs(pairs)\nprint((pairs, s))\n```\n```output\n([(1, 2008), (2, 1004), (4, 502), (251, 8), (502, 4), (1004, 2), (2008, 1)], [2009, 1006, 506, 255, 506, 1006, 2009])\n```\nThe pairs of factors \\((p, q)\\) that satisfy \\(p \\cdot q = 2008\\) and their corresponding sums are:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n    (1, 2008) & \\rightarrow 2009 \\\\\n    (2, 1004) & \\rightarrow 1006 \\\\\n    (4, 502) & \\rightarrow 506 \\\\\n    (251, 8) & \\rightarrow 255 \\\\\n    (502, 4) & \\rightarrow 506 \\\\\n    (1004, 2) & \\rightarrow 1006 \\\\\n    (2008, 1) & \\rightarrow 2009 \\\\\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nFrom these, the smallest positive sum \\( b \\) is 2009, which corresponds to the pair \\((1, 2008)\\).\n\nTherefore, the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2009}\n\\]",
